// PARAM: --analysis interval
// Rejection case, the converse of 13-void_procedure_returns_value.vimp. A
// procedure declaring a return kind must deliver a value on every path that
// can leave it, because its callers may bind the result; the else arm here
// falls off the end with nothing to assign. A loop never counts as returning
// either, since it may not be entered.
int32 f(int32 n) {
  if (n < 1) { return n } else { skip }
}
void main() {
  int32 a;
  a := f(1)
}
